     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif\">Hello, I have made an update to v0.64.0.<br><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif\">There was an error in some situations when returning permutation p-values by the function &quot;SPM&quot;. This has been corrected.<br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif\">&quot;plot_rich_norm&quot; should now work for more than 2 groups. It will also work with multi-subject data; it collapses across &quot;Study.ID&quot; and plots the group means<br><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif\">You can see the changes on the <a href=\"https://github.com/cwatson/brainGraph/commit/d8ce16a24a892f29241107d8cdee41e5dbf424e4?short_path=8312ad0#diff-8312ad0561ef661716b48d09478362f3\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/cwatson/brainGraph/commit/d8ce16a24a892f29241107d8cdee41e5dbf424e4?short_path%3D8312ad0%23diff-8312ad0561ef661716b48d09478362f3&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792488207082000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EsEay4_tIRMUb_NZBeiYI\">Github page</a>.<br><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif\">Chris<br></div></div>\r\n"
